  "title": "Multiple Object Monitoring (EEG)",
  "description": "This dataset comprises EEG recordings from 30 participants who performed a Multiple Object Monitoring (MOM) task, designed to investigate attentional tracking of multiple moving objects. The data were collected to examine the neural correlates underlying dynamic attention allocation and object monitoring processes. The dataset is intended for use in cognitive neuroscience research on visual attention and working memory.",
